    The path data below is copied byte for byte out of the frontend's `public/assets/mandala.svg`
    — the uploaded master the site itself draws from, and the one its `models/mandalaPath.ts`
    carries the same note about: DO NOT REDRAW OR EDIT IT BY HAND. A hand-made approximation of the
    mandala is a second mandala, and the two drift, exactly as a hand-drawn brand mark would.

    What has changed is the PAINT, not the geometry. The master ships marigold at 0.2 opacity
    because on the site it sits behind white sections as a watermark; on this indigo panel that is
    invisible. So the curve is declared once in <defs> and stamped twice by <use>, with the colour,
    size and position of each stamp coming from the stylesheet. Two stamps of one definition rather
    than two copies of the path keeps 5.5KB of curve data in the document exactly once.

    Decorative, so every element here is aria-hidden: the headline beside it already says what this
    screen is, and "image" announced twice is noise to somebody listening to the page.
--}}
